  <prompt>Rewrite `SPAARKE-FIELD-MAPPING-FRAMEWORK.md` and `FIELD-MAPPING-ADMIN-GUIDE.md` for the shipped behaviour: server-side, fill-only at create; `/push` Copy-only by sync mode; "use a quick view when the child only needs to show the parent's value"; never define OOB relationship mappings on rule-owned fields. Update the registry rows I-3 and I-5 to done and I-6 in `DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md`. Update the root `CLAUDE.md` §17 Field Mapping row and §13 entry point, and add a `.claude/CHANGELOG.md` entry. The root CLAUDE.md and .claude/CHANGELOG.md edits MUST be made by the MAIN SESSION; a sub-agent cannot write under .claude/ and root CLAUDE.md edits are applied by the main session.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE technical writer / platform developer; docs follow the docs-architecture and docs-guide skills.</role>
  <goal>The docs describe what shipped (verified against code), the invariant registry marks I-3/I-5 done and I-6 current, and the root pointers send agents to the right documents.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>spec.md FR-28 (docs part). Code wins; docs lag: write only behaviour verified in code or in the live checks of tasks 040 and 053, and the matrix from task 060. DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md is ALSO edited by PR #1911 and UAC-r2 PR #2110 (merge-aware: re-read the latest merged file, confine edits to I-3/I-5/I-6 rows, run /conflict-check). Root CLAUDE.md §13 and §17 rows follow root CLAUDE.md §18 maintainer notes (read the HTML comment at the top before editing).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">docs/architecture/SPAARKE-FIELD-MAPPING-FRAMEWORK.md (rewrite; keep the task 001 semantics table accurate)</file>
      <file role="modify">docs/guides/FIELD-MAPPING-ADMIN-GUIDE.md (fill-only, push and sync mode, quick view advice, no OOB relationship maps on rule-owned fields)</file>
      <file role="modify">docs/architecture/DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md (registry rows I-3/I-5 done; I-6 updated; matrix from task 060 stays)</file>
      <file role="modify">CLAUDE.md (root; MAIN SESSION ONLY: §17 "Touch field mapping or set-regarding" row and §13 entry point for the canonical engine/RecordCreationService)</file>
      <file role="modify">.claude/CHANGELOG.md (MAIN SESSION ONLY: one entry for the CLAUDE.md pointer change)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/field-mapping-server-write-path-r1/spec.md FR-28; notes/decisions.md; notes/w5-live-check.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="040" status="pending">Push behaviour as shipped (Copy-only, sync mode, fixed error text).</dependency>
      <dependency task="053" status="pending">W5 behaviour as verified live.</dependency>
      <dependency task="060" status="pending">Ownership matrix and exception decisions.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §3">Scope: .claude/ and root CLAUDE.md. Sub-agents cannot write under .claude/ ("Edit denied on .claude/..." is the boundary working). The MAIN SESSION applies the root CLAUDE.md and .claude/CHANGELOG.md edits; a sub-agent drafts the exact text in notes/ and stops.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §2">Scope: truth. Every statement in the rewritten docs is verified against code or recorded evidence; no aspirational text; remove statements about the client engine and quick-create flags that are now false.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project (merge-aware)">Scope: shared doc. DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md is also edited by PR #1911 and UAC-r2 PR #2110; edit only the I-3/I-5/I-6 rows on the latest merge; never overwrite their sections; run /conflict-check.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §18">Scope: CLAUDE.md edits. Read the maintainer notes in the HTML comment at the top of the file before editing; keep rows concise; add the CHANGELOG entry in the same change.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-002">Scope: wording. Docs state the server is the single owner of each invariant and that OOB relationship maps, plugins, flows and business rules do not own invariants.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Field mapping documentation; write-path registry</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-002-thin-plugins.md</file>
