    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare MINIMAL rigor; state that root CLAUDE.md and .claude/CHANGELOG.md edits run in the main session; read spec FR-28 and the evidence notes; /conflict-check on the three docs.</step>
    <step order="1">Rewrite the two field-mapping docs from verified behaviour; keep the semantics table (task 001) and add fill-only, sync mode, push, repair pass, quick-view advice, OOB-map prohibition.</step>
    <step order="2">Update I-3/I-5 (done) and I-6 rows in the write-path doc on the latest merge.</step>
    <step order="3">Draft the root CLAUDE.md §17 and §13 text and the CHANGELOG entry in notes/ (sub-agent) and have the MAIN SESSION apply them to CLAUDE.md and .claude/CHANGELOG.md.</step>
    <step order="4">Grep the repo docs for stale statements (client mapping, applyFieldMappings, quick create on) and fix or list them.</step>
    <step order="5">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="6">Document any deviation in projects/field-mapping-server-write-path-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a doc statement cannot be verified against code or live evidence, do not write it: STOP and escalate or mark it open in notes/ per CLAUDE.md §6.</trigger>
    <trigger>If PR #1911 or #2110 restructured the registry rows so I-3/I-5/I-6 no longer exist as such, stop and ask before reshaping.</trigger>
  </escalation>

